-2-nuclear-forces-and-radioactivity", "page_title": "22.2 Nuclear Forces and Radioactivity", "page_uuid": "f2efbd0d-73fa-4ee4-94d0-8d73c75fc534", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-08", "role": null, "source": "openstax", "source_url": "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/22-2-nuclear-forces-and-radioactivity#Table_22_01", "summary": "Table containing three columns: Proton mass, Neutron mass, and electron mass; and two rows: Kilograms and Atomic mass units.", "table_number": "22.1"}
{"archive_version": "20260604.144757", "book_slug": "physics", "book_state": "live", "book_title": "Physics", "book_uuid": "cce64fde-f448-43b8-ae88-27705cceb0da", "book_version": "dfdfd7a", "caption": "Comparing the Electromagnetic and Strong Forces", "content_url": "https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/contents/cce64fde-f448-43b8-ae88-27705cceb0da@dfdfd7a:f2efbd0d-73fa-4ee4-94d0-8d73c75fc534.json", "context": null, "element_id": "Table_22_02", "has_thead": true, "header_cells": [{"col": 0, "row": 0, "scope": "col", "text": ""}, {"col": 1, "row": 0, "scope": "col", "text": "Range of Force"}, {"col": 2, "row": 0, "scope": "col", "text": "Direction"}, {"col": 3, "row": 0, "scope": "col", "text": "Nucleon Interaction"}, {"col": 4, "row": 0, "scope": "col", "text": "Magnitude of Force"}], "html": "<table id=\"Table_22_02\" data-summary=\"Table with four columns: Range of force, direction, nucleon interaction, magnitude of force; and two rows: Electromagnetic force and strong nuclear force.\"><thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" />\n<th scope=\"col\">Range of Force</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Direction</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Nucleon Interaction</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Magnitude of Force</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Electromagnetic Force</strong></td>\n<td>Long range, though decreasing by 1/r<sup>2</sup></td>\n<td>Repulsive</td>\n<td>Proton –proton repulsion</td>\n<td>Relatively small</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Strong Nuclear Force</strong></td>\n<td>Very short range, essentially zero at 1 femtometer</td>\n<td>Attractive</td>\n<td>Attraction between any two nucleons</td>\n<td>100 times greater than the electromagnetic force</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>", "id": "openstax/physics/22-2-nuclear-forces-and-radioactivity/tab-002", "index_on_page": 2, "is_layout": false, "kind": "table", "license_name": "Creative Commons Attribution License", "license_url": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "n_cols": 5, "n_rows": 3, "page_slug": "22-2-nuclear-forces-and-radioactivity", "page_title": "22.2 Nuclear Forces and Radioactivity", "page_uuid": "f2efbd0d-73fa-4ee4-94d0-8d73c75fc534", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-08", "role": null, "source": "openstax", "source_url": "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/22-2-nuclear-forces-and-radioactivity#Table_22_02", "summary": "Table with four columns: Range of force, direction, nucleon interaction, magnitude of force; and two rows: Electromagnetic force and strong nuclear force.", "table_number": "22.2"}
